<title>USA: Calpine Corp adopts rights plan.</title>
<headline>Calpine Corp adopts rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Calif 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calpine Corp said Monday that its board had adopted a stockholder rights plan if anyone tries to acquire 15 percent or more of its common stock.</p>
<p>Each right represents a contingent right to buy a fractional share of a newly created series of Calpine preferred stock for $80, the company said.</p>
<p>If the company is acquired after someone buys 15 percent or more of its common stock, each right will let holders buy fractional shares of its preferred stock or common shares at a market value of twice such exercise price, the company said.</p>
<p>The company said the rights expire June 18, 2007.</p>
</text>
